WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:03.696
Take a ride in Emily Dickinson's chariot.

00:00:03.696 --> 00:00:06.866
But beware... there's no turning back.

00:00:08.035 --> 00:00:12.472
"Because I could not stop for Death"
by Emily Dickinson

00:00:25.018 --> 00:00:30.348
Because I could not stop for Death –
He kindly stopped for me –

00:00:43.278 --> 00:00:48.067
The Carriage held but just Ourselves –
And Immortality.

00:00:49.074 --> 00:00:55.170
We slowly drove – He knew no haste
And I had put away

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:59.900
My labor and my leisure too,
For His Civility –

00:01:00.873 --> 00:01:04.573
We passed the School, 
where Children strove

00:01:04.573 --> 00:01:11.402
At Recess – in the Ring –
We passed the Fields of Gazing Grain –

00:01:11.402 --> 00:01:13.662
We passed the Setting Sun –

00:01:14.991 --> 00:01:21.581
Or rather – He passed Us –
The Dews drew quivering and Chill –

00:01:22.551 --> 00:01:27.541
For only Gossamer, my Gown –
My Tippet – only Tulle –

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:35.604
We paused before a House that seemed
A Swelling of the Ground –

00:01:35.604 --> 00:01:41.454
The Roof was scarcely visible –
The Cornice – in the Ground –

00:01:56.203 --> 00:02:03.187
Since then – 'tis Centuries – and yet
Feels shorter than the Day

00:02:03.187 --> 00:02:09.437
I first surmised the Horses' Heads
Were toward Eternity –

